1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This is messed up.
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriages to Anna and Olaug are concurrent, as shown by children born to both during the same year, and the two families didn't live on the same farm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Olaug lived on Maarud, and the farm came to her from her first husband, Tarald. Ivar Flevig married her.
2 CONT * Anna lived on Flevig/Fløvig/Fløvik, and the farm may have come from his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT If so, then Anna's Iver may have been the son of these parents. But we need to find the origins of Anna and Olaug's husband to be sure.
2 CONT
2 CONT After looking thoroughly into the church book, Iver and Sven looks almost indistinguishable. Brothers Peder and Swen were confirmed on the same day.
2 CONT
2 CONT It turns out Anna was married to Sven. Because Sven and Iver looks almost indistinguishable in the church book, and extra couple was assumed to exist. There's another couple that was mixed in here. Iver Flevik that's actually Iver
2 CONC  Nilsen Fløvik married to Anna Kristensdatter Volen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grete Brustad Nilsen believes Sven and Anna were married, and that seems to fit when Reading the straps we found in the church books.
2 CONT
2 CONT We already know Martha Østensvig got it wrong by not realizing Olaug's and Anna's husband were not the same man. We have no proof Olaug's husband was Svens brother. We just don't know how else he came by living at Fløvik.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaug's husband seems to be the one who married Pernille.
2 CONT
2 CONT There's no hint at where Anna and Sven ended up and we can't find proff of where the children who lived to adulthood ended up. We know Erik was confirmed at Ledeng. That's all we know so far.
